{"skill":{"slug":"dragon-ppt-maker","displayName":"PPT制作"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1772352557960,"changelog":"初始版本","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"ppt_maker.py","size":23471,"sha256":"a1528d45e75b15850f6424d491c7be403db1b287235f9706659ecd33683a0a62","contentType":"text/plain"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":1727,"sha256":"97e94024c56b79270c67a92a6b1147e83d5a8577ed93d303ca704adf091cf908","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1819,"sha256":"ab286ecaf952c7b90c2549fca596937cab6347de437caed87177e7aab1a4965a","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789093707742,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"45f2e9a3caef9879ea79219497f5ee310001006bee7665d3e78e856bf8ca93ab","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/45f2e9a3caef9879ea79219497f5ee310001006bee7665d3e78e856bf8ca93ab","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: dragon-ppt-maker\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe `ppt_maker.py` script is suspicious due to an arbitrary file write vulnerability. The `--output` command-line argument is directly used as the filename for `prs.save()`, allowing a user or an agent to specify an arbitrary file path (e.g., via path traversal) to write the generated PPTX file to any location on the file system where the process has write permissions. While the content written is a PPTX file, this lack of input sanitization for file paths is a significant security flaw.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779168254247},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":24,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789093707742},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is a straightforward PowerPoint generation helper with ordinary local file output and no evidence of hidden execution, exfiltration, persistence, or privilege escalation.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Most output paths are user-controlled, but the --openclaw mode saves to a hard-coded Windows Desktop path, which is purpose-aligned but should be disclosed and made configurable.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The install command uses unpinned pip dependencies, which is a normal but improvable supply-chain posture for a small Python utility.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Instructions and CLI text are Chinese-only, which may limit usability for non-Chinese users but does not create a security concern by itself.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The artifact does not install services, schedule tasks, alter agent behavior, request elevated privileges, or write persistent configuration beyond generated presentation files.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The documented purpose is to create styled PowerPoint files, and the Python code implements slide generation using python-pptx and Pillow without unrelated capabilities.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install in a virtual environment, consider pinning python-pptx and Pillow, and review or override output paths before running --openclaw because that mode writes to a fixed Desktop path on Windows.","findings":"[SQP-3] expected: The Chinese-only documentation and help text are a locale/usability issue rather than evidence of unsafe behavior.\n[SQP-2] expected: Generating a PPTX file is expected for this skill, but the hard-coded Desktop path in --openclaw mode is under-scoped and users should choose or review output locations.\n[T08] expected: python-pptx and Pillow match the presentation-generation purpose; unpinned versions are a supply-chain caution, not evidence of malicious intent in the artifact.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789093707742}}}}}